{#  What a picture says about a LOOK, in this app's own words.

    The colours are worked out from the pixels and are not asked for
    here -- arithmetic does that better and needs no provider. What a
    model can do that pixels cannot is name the FEEL: whether the type
    is serif or geometric, whether the corners are sharp or soft,
    whether things sit flat on the page or float above it.

    Every answer is checked against these lists on the way back, because
    a model naming a font this app cannot load is a look that silently
    falls back to nothing. This is the polite half of that. #}
